<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE article [
<!ENTITY % coursevars SYSTEM "../course-vars.ent">
%coursevars;
]>
<subsection xml:id="report" component="graduate">
  <title>Excursion Report and Presentation</title>
  <p>
    Several sections of <pubtitle>&book;</pubtitle> are labeled <q>Excursion.</q>
    Each excursion introduces a topic that lies beyond the core material of the course.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each graduate student will choose one excursion, study it independently, and
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>submit a written report on it, and</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>give a 10-minute presentation on it to the class.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <p>
    Each student must choose a different excursion, and the choice must be approved by the instructor.
    The report must be typed and written in your own words; it should state the main definitions and results of the excursion, work through at least one example, and explain at least one proof.
    Due dates for the choice of topic, the report, and the presentation will be announced in class.
  </p>
</subsection>
